    "answer": {
      "short": "Six cosine curves with period $2\\pi$, amplitudes $1,2,3$, and common zeros $\\frac\\pi2,\\frac{3\\pi}2$. Negative coefficients reflect the corresponding curves in the $x$-axis.",
      "worked": "For $y=a\\cos x$, plot $(0,a)$, $(\\frac\\pi2,0)$, $(\\pi,-a)$, $(\\frac{3\\pi}2,0)$ and $(2\\pi,a)$ for $a=1,-1,2,-2,3,-3$. Join each set smoothly on the same axes. Each curve has amplitude $|a|$ and period $2\\pi$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": [
